A chalkboard example uses the program below:
console.log(1);
setTimeout(() => console.log(700), 0);
console.log(3);
On this input, what sequence is printed?

Check 0701: The team wants to know what this code logs:
try {
  throw new Error('bad ' + 701);
} catch (e) {
  console.log('caught');
} finally {
  console.log('done');
}
From this trace, what two words appear in the output?

A test harness runs these statements in order:
const text = '{"n":702}';
console.log(JSON.parse(text).n);
In this run, explain what this code prints and why that value follows from the language rules.

